        "finalText":  "I\u0027ll start by reading the required files to understand the codebase.\r\nNow I have a full picture. Let me start with tests and the pure helper.\r\nI accidentally removed the Quota header. Restoring it.\r\nDone. All green: `npx vitest run src/renderer` (742 passed) and `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.web.json --composite false` (zero errors).\n\nWhat changed\n- `state/formatTime.ts`: added `isSleeping(runtime)` and `activityLabel` now returns `\"Sleeping\"` (wins over `\"Exited\"`/activity). Tests added.\n- `settings/sleepValidation.ts` (+test): pure `clampSleepMinutes`/`parseSleepMinutes`.\n- `settings/AutomationSection.tsx`: bordered \"Sleep idle sessions\" card — Switch (`aria-label=\"Sleep idle sessions\"`, `sleep.enabled`), number input \"Sleep after (minutes)\" (`sleep.afterMinutes`, clamped 1–1440, disabled while off), helper text, inline validation error, all persisted via `updateSettings({ sleep: {...} })` like Quota.\n- `Sidebar/SessionCard.tsx`, `hub/HubCard.tsx`: sleeping → Moon icon in place of the dot (`role=\"img\"` aria-label \"Sleeping\", muted token), card dimmed via `opacity-60`; no handler/activation changes.\n- `Sidebar/SessionContextMenu.tsx`, `hub/HubCardMenu.tsx`, `shell/Tab.tsx`: `Sleep` (Moon) → `window.api.sleepSession(id)` for running/awake; `Wake up` (Sun) for sleeping, reusing the existing select/open/activate callbacks. Tab also shows a Moon indicator.\n- Wired in `GroupSection.tsx`, `StatusSection.tsx`, `HubColumn.tsx`; `shell/tabStatus.ts` gained optional `TabModel.sleeping`.\n- `settings/MANUAL_TEST.md`: added the Sleep checklist.\n\nOPEN QUESTIONS\n- No new prop is needed from `App.tsx` — menus call `window.api.sleepSession(id)` directly and wake via existing activate callbacks.\n- I had to touch files outside the listed scope: `hub/HubColumn.tsx` (menu wiring), `shell/tabStatus.ts` (optional `TabModel.sleeping`, required for \"Wake up\" on tabs), and `Sidebar/StatusSection.tsx` (renders the same sidebar card as `GroupSection`; left unwired it would silently lack Sleep/Wake in status grouping). Flagging in case parallel workers own them.\n- `sleepSession` rejections are swallowed (`.catch(() =\u003e undefined)`); no renderer error surface exists for these menu actions. Say the word if you want them surfaced.",
